\tableofcontents

\section usdSolid_overview Overview

UsdSolid provides native, mathematically-exact solid boundary-representation
(B-rep) geometry for OpenUSD. Its single concrete schema, UsdSolidBrepArray,
stores one or more Breps in a packed, flat, array-based representation built on
Weiler's Radial Edge data model, so it can represent manifold solids,
non-manifold solids, sheet bodies, and wireframes in a kernel-neutral form.

Unlike UsdGeomMesh, which is a fixed-resolution approximation, a UsdSolid stores
the exact source surfaces and curves (currently NURBS, in double precision) and
can be re-tessellated to any fidelity on demand. This makes it suitable as a CAD
reference and transport representation that maps cleanly onto PRC (ISO 14739-1),
STEP (ISO 10303), and Parasolid topology.

\note UsdSolid is an active OpenUSD proposal (AOUSD PR #109) and is not yet a
ratified Core schema. Attribute names, packing conventions, and rules may change
as the AOUSD Geometry Working Group aligns on a design.

\section usdSolid_schemas Schemas

\subsection usdSolid_brepArray BrepArray

UsdSolidBrepArray is an IsA Gprim (deriving from UsdGeomGprim) that stores one or
more Breps as parallel, flat arrays on a single prim. Topology (regions, shells,
faces, loops, edges, edgeuses, vertices) is carried by the \c region:, \c shell:,
\c face:, \c loop:, \c edgeuse:, \c edge:, and \c vertex: array families;
geometry (NURBS surfaces, 3D curves, trim curves, and points) is carried by
\c brep: -prefixed applied API schemas.

\subsection usdSolid_geomApis Geometry API Schemas

Per-face surfaces and per-edge curves are supplied by applied API schemas,
selected per element via \c face:surfaceType and \c edge:curveType:
 - Surfaces: UsdSolidBrepSurfaceNurbAPI, UsdSolidBrepSurfacePlaneAPI,
   UsdSolidBrepSurfaceCylinderAPI, UsdSolidBrepSurfaceConeAPI,
   UsdSolidBrepSurfaceSphereAPI, UsdSolidBrepSurfaceTorusAPI
 - 3D edge curves: UsdSolidBrepCurve3dNurbAPI, UsdSolidBrepCurve3dLineAPI,
   UsdSolidBrepCurve3dCircleAPI, UsdSolidBrepCurve3dEllipseAPI
 - Trim curves and points: UsdSolidBrepCurveUvNurbAPI (2D pcurves),
   UsdSolidBrepPointAPI (vertex points)

\section usdSolid_userguide User Guide

For B-rep concepts, the Radial Edge data model, the flat-array packing
conventions, a worked authoring example, tessellation, and the full set of rules
and restrictions, see the UsdSolid user guide.

*/
